dxil-spirv: Copy long vectors through ray payloads as arrays.

For vkd3d-proton 3.0.1 (subprojects/dxil-spirv 62dbb07). Ported from
Autodesk-Inventor-for-Linux PR #3 (krokosik, written with Codex and
GPT-6.1-Sol, patches/gpu/vkd3d-ray-payload.patch for 2.14.1); the hunk
that only replaced get_effective_storage_class() with the same lookup is
left out. LGPL-2.1-or-later like vkd3d-proton.

DXC copies a float3x4 in a ray payload as a <12 x float> load and store.
dxil-spirv 3.0.1 emits that as a 12-component OpTypeVector, which SPIR-V
does not allow without SPV_EXT_long_vector (RADV in Mesa 26.2 does not
offer it); vkCreateRayTracingPipelinesKHR then faults in the driver, as
it does for Inventor 2027's GPU ray tracer on an RX 6400. Vectors longer
than 4 become arrays, and loads and stores through such a pointer are
reshaped component by component instead of bitcast.

Checked with original synthetic shaders (gpu/vkd3d-proton/tests/): without
the patch spirv-val rejects all six ("Illegal number of components (12)
for TypeVector"), with it all six validate.

